<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kabalega</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1853–1923</span> · Also known as Chwa II Kabalega, Kabarega</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kabalega was omukama (king) of Bunyoro in western Uganda from 1870 to 1899. He built a standing army, the abarusura, revived Bunyoro's power, reconquered Toro in 1876 and resisted the advance of Buganda. From 1891 he fought the British and their Ganda allies in a long <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> war until his capture in 1899, after which he was exiled to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seychelles">Seychelles</a>. Uganda honours him as a hero of resistance.</p></div>
